            <ArticleTitle>Acute angle-closure glaucoma after albuterol nebulizer treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report acute angle-closure glaucoma associated with albuterol nebulizer treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case report and review of the relevant literature.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In a 75-year-old woman with asthma, acute angle-closure glaucoma in the right eye was probably caused by local absorption of albuterol after nebulizer administration.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">As albuterol is widely used in the management of patients with asthma, increased awareness by health care professionals of the potential for acute angle-closure glaucoma secondary to albuterol may decrease the incidence of this complication.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
